{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506532-question-regarding-light-weapons-merit","id":1506532,"title":"Question regarding Light Weapons Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-26T14:35:08-07:00","id":1506532,"title":"Question regarding Light Weapons Merit","content":"For the Thrust ability, if you're using a weapon that already has a damage rating of 0, can you still swap it out for the initiative bonus?<br /> <br /> Also, Feint mentions something about boosting how Feinting works, but I can't find rules for feinting anywhere. What are the rules for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 03-26-2023, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T01:55:08-07:00","id":1506615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506532-question-regarding-light-weapons-merit#post1506532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Thrust ability, if you're using a weapon that already has a damage rating of 0, can you still swap it out for the initiative bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Rapidity? I'd say you can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Feint mentions something about boosting how Feinting works, but I can't find rules for feinting anywhere. What are the rules for this? </div> </div> </div>I believe this is a regular attack action with the light weapon that you nominate to be a Feint and therefore do no damage but it then empowers your next attack.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T03:49:56-07:00","id":1506619,"title":"","content":"Generally, the rules don't side with allowing you to sacrifice something you have zero in; it's not really a sacrifice at that point. So from a technical standpoint I would say Rapidity doesn't work with 0 damage weapons. That said, considering the nature of the style, from a fun and balance perspective, I think interpreting it anyway would be a good thing.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you're talking about in the Feint maneuver. It doesn't say anything about boosting feinting. It has it's own rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T04:40:41-07:00","id":1506620,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I did mean Rapidity. Considering the Merit only works on weapons that have a damage rating of 2 or lower it's not like the weapons have much of a damage rating to sacrifice anyway. Sacrificing a +0 rating seems in keeping with the Merit.<br /> <br /> As for Feint, I must have an older version of the CoD rulebook, because in mine it simply says you can distract an opponent for a cleaner, more effective strike, then gives an example. It doesn't actually say any of the mechanics of how it's meant to work. I thought it just enhanced some kind of feint manoeuvre. It even says in the example &quot;if Feinting with a two damage weapon...&quot; Since the Feinting is capitalized I figured it was referencing a generic manoeuvre or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T09:05:56-07:00","id":1506630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506532-question-regarding-light-weapons-merit?p=1506620#post1506620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Feint, I must have an older version of the CoD rulebook, because in mine it simply says you can distract an opponent for a cleaner, more effective strike, then gives an example. It doesn't actually say any of the mechanics of how it's meant to work. I thought it just enhanced some kind of feint manoeuvre. It even says in the example &quot;if Feinting with a two damage weapon...&quot; Since the Feinting is capitalized I figured it was referencing a generic manoeuvre or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feint is simply poorly worded. It's not referring to enhancing a universal mechanic, but simply introducing a unique maneuver it enables. With Light Weapons 3, you can perform the Feint maneuver, which is better explained: when you Feint, instead of dealing damage, you apply what damage you would have dealt as a Defense penalty to your opponent on your next attack, and you apply your Feint successes as bonus damage on that attack as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}